{%- comment -%}
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  reviews-before-after.liquid
  Skingenetix / Claude Code — created 2026-08-27

  WHY THIS EXISTS
  A customer review slide needs six things at once: a before/after pair, the customer's name, a verified badge, a
  star rating, a review title, the review body, and a link to the product reviewed. Every stock Impact section was
  read before this file was written and none carries more than five of the six:

    testimonials          — name, rating, title, body, native carousel; but its image is an AVATAR, rendered at
                            `sizes: 40px, 56px` with a srcset topping out at 168w. A before/after pair is impossible
                            there, and there is no per-block link.
    multi-column          — image, title, body, link; no name, no rating, and it only carousels below `md`.
    media-with-text       — image, title, body, link; no rating, no carousel of any kind.
    before-after-image    — two images and a drag-to-compare slider; no name, rating, title, body or link.
    slideshow             — a real carousel with one image and one button; no rating, no name.

  WHAT IS REUSED RATHER THAN REBUILT
  The carousel is NOT custom. It is the theme's own `<scroll-carousel>` element plus the theme's own `scrollbar`
  snippet, exactly as `sections/testimonials.liquid` uses them — same `scroll-area bleed` classes, same
  `is-scrollable` gate at more than three blocks, same breakpoints, same prev/next circle-buttons. So the arrows,
  the progress bar, the snap behaviour and the Safari fallbacks all come from the theme. No external library is
  loaded (Hairgenetix pulls Swiper 11 off a CDN for the equivalent component; that is not needed here).
  The star row is the theme's `icon` snippet with `rating-star`, the same markup `testimonials` renders.

  WHY THE TEXT IS ALL `text` SETTINGS
  Shopify exposes every text setting of a section stored in a page template as a translatable resource of type
  ONLINE_STORE_THEME_JSON_TEMPLATE, keyed
      section.page.<template>.json.<section-id>.<block-id>.<setting-id>:<hash>
  so the labels, names, titles and the product link text all appear in Translate & Adapt with no app configuration.
  (The store runs Shopify's own Translate & Adapt. Langify is NOT installed, despite older docs.)
  This is why the BEFORE/AFTER labels are DOM text and must never be baked into the image pixels — the four images
  on this page in August 2026 had them burnt in, and pixels cannot be translated.

  THE IMAGE CONTRACT
  `image` is ONE file holding both frames, split at exactly 50%, and the whole pair is SQUARE (1:1) — so each half
  is a portrait rectangle, half as wide as it is tall. The before label sits over the left half and the after label
  over the right half at fixed percentages, so a master that is not an even 50/50 split will misplace them.

  ADDITIVE ONLY — this is a new file. No core theme file is modified.
  CSS is scoped to #shopify-section-{{ section.id }}, the pattern the theme's own sections use.
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- if section.blocks.size > 0 -%}
  {%- render 'section-spacing-collapsing' -%}

  <style>
    /* Breakpoints mirror sections/testimonials.liquid so this section keeps the same rhythm as the
       theme's own card carousel. 1 card up to 700px, 2 to 1150px, 3 above it. */
    #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} {
      --rbac-items-per-row: 1;
      --rbac-item-width: 74vw;
      --rbac-radius: 10px;
    }

    @media screen and (min-width: 700px) {
      #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} {
        --rbac-items-per-row: 2;
        --rbac-item-width: 52vw;
      }
    }

    @media screen and (min-width: 1000px) {
      #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} {
        --rbac-item-width: 36vw;
      }
    }

    @media screen and (min-width: 1150px) {
      #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} {
        --rbac-items-per-row: 3;
        --rbac-item-width: calc(100% / 3 - (var(--grid-gutter) / 3 * 2));
      }
    }

    #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .rbac-list {
      display: grid;
      grid: auto / auto-flow var(--rbac-item-width);
      gap: var(--grid-gutter);
      /* `stretch`, so every card in the row is as tall as the tallest and the product line lands
         on one baseline — reviews are never the same length, and at 15 cards the spread was 630px
         to 749px. Safe here only because .rbac-card__media carries a fixed `aspect-ratio: 1 / 1`,
         so the picture cannot grow with the card and the labels positioned against it cannot be
         pushed off it. The sibling `research-before-after` section had exactly that bug and needs
         `align-self: start` for the opposite reason: its media box has no aspect-ratio. */
      align-items: stretch;
    }

    #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .scrollbar {
      --text-color: {{ section.settings.text_color.rgb | default: settings.text_color.rgb }};
    }

    /* ---- prev/next on the left and right edges, vertically centred on the cards ----------------
       This is the theme's own `floating-controls-container` pattern, not a new one: theme.css
       already gives `.floating-controls-container .circle-button` `position: absolute` and
       `top: calc(50% - 24px)`, and places the first button at `left: var(--spacing-5)` and the
       last at `right: var(--spacing-5)` — with the four `:lang()` variants that flip them for
       right-to-left locales, which matters here because nine are planned.

       Two things about it have to be corrected, and both are why this block exists.

       1. The container must wrap ONLY the track. `top: 50%` is 50% of the positioned ancestor, so
          wrapping the whole `.scrollable-with-controls` would centre the buttons against the track
          PLUS the progress bar beneath it, and they would sit low.
       2. The theme reveals them on hover only —
          `.floating-controls-container:hover .is-scrollable ~ .circle-button:not([disabled])`.
          On a review carousel the controls are the only cue that there are twelve more cards, so
          they are always on here. Note the theme's rule needs `is-scrollable` on the sibling track
          or nothing appears, hover or not; the theme's own JS adds that class from real overflow.

       Disabled is shown, not hidden: at the start the prev button greys out rather than vanishing,
       so the pair does not jump into existence on the first click. */
    #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .floating-controls-container .is-scrollable ~ .circle-button {
      opacity: 1;
      visibility: visible;
      transform: scale(1);
    }

    #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .floating-controls-container .is-scrollable ~ .circle-button[disabled] {
      opacity: 0.35;
    }

    /* Below 700px a card is 74vw, so an edge button would sit on top of the photograph. Touch
       swipes the track anyway, and the progress bar still shows there is more. */
    @media screen and (max-width: 699px) {
      #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .floating-controls-container > .circle-button { display: none; }
    }

    #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .rbac-card {
      background: {{ section.settings.card_background }};
      color: {{ section.settings.card_text_color }};
      border-radius: var(--rbac-radius);
      overflow: hidden;
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
    }

    /* The master is a 1:1 diptych, so the media box is square and the two halves are portrait.
       `aspect-ratio` rather than the image's own ratio, so a master that is slightly off does not
       drag the card out of line with its siblings. */
    #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .rbac-card__media {
      position: relative;
      aspect-ratio: 1 / 1;
      line-height: 0;
      background: rgb(var(--border-color) / 0.35);
    }

    #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .rbac-card__media img {
      width: 100%;
      height: 100%;
      object-fit: cover;
      display: block;
    }

    /* A seam between the two frames, so the pair reads as two photographs rather than one wide one. */
    #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .rbac-card__seam {
      position: absolute;
      inset-block: 0;
      left: 50%;
      width: 2px;
      transform: translateX(-1px);
      background: {{ section.settings.card_background }};
      pointer-events: none;
    }

    /* Contrast is bought with a local chip behind each label, never a wash over the whole picture —
       a flat overlay dulls the photograph instead of fixing legibility. */
    #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .rbac-card__label {
      position: absolute;
      top: var(--spacing-2-5);
      margin: 0;
      padding: 0.35em 0.75em;
      border-radius: 999px;
      background: {{ section.settings.label_background }};
      color: {{ section.settings.label_text_color }};
      font-size: 0.7rem;
      font-weight: 600;
      letter-spacing: 0.05em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      line-height: 1.2;
      white-space: nowrap;
      max-width: 44%;
      overflow: hidden;
      text-overflow: ellipsis;
      backdrop-filter: blur(3px);
      -webkit-backdrop-filter: blur(3px);
    }

    #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .rbac-card__label--before { left: 3%; }
    #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .rbac-card__label--after { left: 53%; }

    #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .rbac-card__body {
      display: flex;
      flex-direction: column;
      padding: var(--spacing-6) var(--spacing-6-5) var(--spacing-7);
      flex: 1 1 auto;
    }

    #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .rbac-card__author {
      margin: 0;
      font-weight: 600;
    }

    #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .rbac-card__verified {
      display: inline-flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: 5px;
      margin: var(--spacing-1-5) 0 0;
      font-size: 0.7rem;
      font-weight: 600;
      letter-spacing: 0.06em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      color: {{ section.settings.verified_color }};
    }

    #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .rbac-card__verified svg { flex: none; }
    #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .rbac-card__rating { margin-top: var(--spacing-2-5); }

    #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .rbac-card__title {
      margin: var(--spacing-3) 0 0;
      font-weight: 600;
      line-height: 1.35;
    }

    #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .rbac-card__text {
      margin-top: var(--spacing-2);
      font-size: 0.9rem;
      line-height: 1.6;
      opacity: 0.82;
    }

    /* Pushed to the bottom so the product line sits on one baseline across cards of unequal copy length. */
    #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .rbac-card__product {
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      gap: var(--spacing-3);
      margin: var(--spacing-4) 0 0;
      padding-top: var(--spacing-4);
      font-size: 0.8rem;
      margin-top: auto;
    }

    /* A pack shot on a white ground, so `contain` rather than `cover`: cropping a bottle to fill
       a square is worse than letterboxing it. The tinted ground keeps a white-on-white pack
       readable as an object. */
    #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .rbac-card__product-thumb {
      flex: none;
      width: 44px;
      height: 44px;
      border-radius: 6px;
      object-fit: contain;
      background: rgb(var(--border-color) / 0.3);
    }

    #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .rbac-card__product-copy { min-width: 0; }

    /* The gap is a margin, not a literal space in the markup. The whitespace-stripping form of
       the surrounding Liquid tags eats any space typed between the prefix and the link, so the
       line rendered as "ReviewingAcetyl Hexapeptide-8..." on the live page. Caught 2026-08-27.
       (Do not write the stripping tag delimiters into a comment here either — Liquid parses
       this file before the browser ever sees it, and a 422 on upload is what that costs.) */
    #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .rbac-card__product .rbac-card__product-prefix {
      display: block;
      opacity: 0.55;
      margin-bottom: 0.15em;
    }

    #shopify-section-{{ section.id }} .rbac-card__product a {
      font-weight: 600;
      text-decoration: underline;
      text-underline-offset: 3px;
    }
  </style>

  <div {% render 'section-properties' %}>
    <div class="section-stack">
      {%- render 'section-header',
        subheading: section.settings.subheading,
        heading: section.settings.title,
        heading_color: section.settings.heading_color,
        content: section.settings.content,
        link_text: section.settings.link_text,
        link_url: section.settings.link_url
      -%}

      <div class="scrollable-with-controls">
        {%- assign scroll_area_id = 'scroll-area-' | append: section.id -%}

        <div class="floating-controls-container">
        <scroll-carousel id="{{ scroll_area_id }}" class="rbac-list scroll-area bleed md:unbleed {% if section.blocks.size > 3 %}is-scrollable{% endif %}">
          {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
            {%- liquid
              assign img = block.settings.image

              assign loading_strategy = nil
              if section.index > 2 or forloop.index > 3
                assign loading_strategy = 'lazy'
              endif
            -%}
            <div class="rbac-card snap-start" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
              <div class="rbac-card__media">
                {%- if img != blank -%}
                  <picture>
                    {%- if block.settings.image_mobile != blank -%}
                      <source
                        media="(max-width: 699px)"
                        srcset="{{ block.settings.image_mobile | image_url: width: 600 }} 600w, {{ block.settings.image_mobile | image_url: width: 900 }} 900w"
                        width="{{ block.settings.image_mobile.width }}"
                        height="{{ block.settings.image_mobile.height }}"
                      >
                    {%- endif -%}
                    {{-
                      img
                      | image_url: width: img.width
                      | image_tag:
                        sizes: '(max-width: 699px) 74vw, (max-width: 1149px) 52vw, 440px',
                        widths: '400,560,700,880,1100,1320',
                        loading: loading_strategy,
                        alt: img.alt
                    -}}
                  </picture>
                  <span class="rbac-card__seam" aria-hidden="true"></span>
                {%- else -%}
                  {{- 'image' | placeholder_svg_tag: 'placeholder' -}}
                {%- endif -%}

                {%- if block.settings.before_label != blank -%}
                  <p class="rbac-card__label rbac-card__label--before">{{ block.settings.before_label | escape }}</p>
                {%- endif -%}
                {%- if block.settings.after_label != blank -%}
                  <p class="rbac-card__label rbac-card__label--after">{{ block.settings.after_label | escape }}</p>
                {%- endif -%}
              </div>

              <div class="rbac-card__body">
                {%- if block.settings.author != blank -%}
                  <p class="rbac-card__author">{{ block.settings.author | escape }}</p>
                {%- endif -%}

                {%- if block.settings.show_verified and block.settings.verified_label != blank -%}
                  <p class="rbac-card__verified">
                    <svg width="13" height="13" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="none" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
                      <path d="M8 1l1.9 1.4 2.3-.2.7 2.2 1.9 1.3-.9 2.2.9 2.2-1.9 1.3-.7 2.2-2.3-.2L8 15l-1.9-1.4-2.3.2-.7-2.2L1.2 10l.9-2.2-.9-2.2 1.9-1.3.7-2.2 2.3.2L8 1z" fill="currentColor"/>
                      <path d="M5.6 8.1l1.7 1.7 3.2-3.4" stroke="{{ section.settings.card_background }}" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
                    </svg>
                    {{ block.settings.verified_label | escape }}
                  </p>
                {%- endif -%}

                {%- if block.settings.show_rating -%}
                  <div class="rating rbac-card__rating">
                    <div class="rating__stars" role="img" aria-label="{{ 'general.rating.info' | t: rating_value: block.settings.rating, rating_max: 5 }}">
                      {%- for i in (1..5) -%}
                        {%- if i <= block.settings.rating -%}
                          {%- render 'icon' with 'rating-star', class: 'rating__star rating__star--full' -%}
                        {%- else -%}
                          {%- render 'icon' with 'rating-star', class: 'rating__star rating__star--empty' -%}
                        {%- endif -%}
                      {%- endfor -%}
                    </div>
                  </div>
                {%- endif -%}

                {%- if block.settings.title != blank -%}
                  <p class="rbac-card__title">{{ block.settings.title | escape }}</p>
                {%- endif -%}

                {%- if block.settings.content != blank -%}
                  <div class="rbac-card__text prose">{{ block.settings.content }}</div>
                {%- endif -%}

                {%- comment -%}
                  The product line resolves from a real product when one is picked, so the thumbnail,
                  the name and the URL all stay correct if the product is renamed or its image
                  changes — and the name is translated by Shopify's own product resource rather than
                  needing a second copy of it here. `product_text` / `product_url` still win when
                  set, because one card points at a collection ("the peptide serum range") and there
                  is no product to pick. `product_image` covers the thumbnail for that same case.
                {%- endcomment -%}
                {%- liquid
                  assign product = block.settings.product

                  assign product_text = block.settings.product_text
                  if product_text == blank and product != blank
                    assign product_text = product.title
                  endif

                  assign product_url = block.settings.product_url
                  if product_url == blank and product != blank
                    assign product_url = product.url
                  endif

                  assign product_thumb = block.settings.product_image
                  if product_thumb == blank and product != blank
                    assign product_thumb = product.featured_image
                  endif
                -%}

                {%- if product_text != blank -%}
                  <div class="rbac-card__product">
                    {%- if product_thumb != blank -%}
                      {{-
                        product_thumb
                        | image_url: width: 132
                        | image_tag:
                          class: 'rbac-card__product-thumb',
                          widths: '44,88,132',
                          sizes: '44px',
                          loading: 'lazy',
                          alt: product_thumb.alt
                      -}}
                    {%- endif -%}
                    <p class="rbac-card__product-copy">
                      {%- if block.settings.product_prefix != blank -%}
                        <span class="rbac-card__product-prefix">{{ block.settings.product_prefix | escape }}</span>
                      {%- endif -%}
                      {%- if product_url != blank -%}
                        <a href="{{ product_url }}">{{ product_text | escape }}</a>
                      {%- else -%}
                        {{ product_text | escape }}
                      {%- endif -%}
                    </p>
                  </div>
                {%- endif -%}
              </div>
            </div>
          {%- endfor -%}
        </scroll-carousel>

          {%- comment -%}
            These are DIRECT SIBLINGS of the track and come after it, with no wrapper. Both the
            theme's reveal rule and its left/right placement depend on it: the reveal is
            `.is-scrollable ~ .circle-button`, a general sibling combinator, and the sides come
            from `:first-of-type` / `:last-of-type` among the container's buttons. Wrap these two
            in a div and they land in the middle, invisible. `aria-controls` is the whole wiring —
            it is how the theme's prev-button / next-button elements find what they scroll.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <button
            is="prev-button"
            class="circle-button circle-button--fill ring group"
            aria-controls="{{ scroll_area_id }}"
            disabled
          >
            <span class="sr-only">{{ 'general.accessibility.previous' | t }}</span>
            <span class="animated-arrow animated-arrow--reverse"></span>
          </button>

          <button
            is="next-button"
            class="circle-button circle-button--fill ring group"
            aria-controls="{{ scroll_area_id }}"
          >
            <span class="sr-only">{{ 'general.accessibility.next' | t }}</span>
            <span class="animated-arrow"></span>
          </button>
        </div>

        {%- comment -%}
          The scrollbar snippet carries `peer-not-scrollable:hidden`, so with three or fewer cards
          — which do not overflow — the arrows and progress bar hide themselves. That is the same
          gate `testimonials` uses, and it is why no block-count test is written here: a count is a
          proxy for the target and this store has twice shipped a bug from scoping on one.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- comment -%}
          `show_buttons: false` — the prev/next pair now lives on the left and right edges of the
          track, so rendering the snippet's own pair underneath would put two identical sets of
          arrows on one carousel. The progress bar stays: it is the only thing that says how far
          through fifteen cards you are, and it is the sole cue on mobile, where the edge buttons
          are hidden.
        {%- endcomment -%}
        {%- assign default_progress = 3.0 | divided_by: section.blocks.size -%}
        {%- render 'scrollbar', observes: scroll_area_id, default_progress: default_progress, show_buttons: false -%}
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
{%- endif -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Review before/after",
  "tag": "section",
  "class": "shopify-section--reviews-before-after",
  "max_blocks": 24,
  "settings": [
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "full_width", "label": "Full width", "default": true },
    { "type": "text", "id": "subheading", "label": "Subheading" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "title", "label": "Heading" },
    { "type": "richtext", "id": "content", "label": "Content" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "link_text", "label": "Link text" },
    { "type": "url", "id": "link_url", "label": "Link URL" },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Colors" },
    { "type": "color", "id": "background", "label": "Background", "default": "#f7f7f7" },
    { "type": "color_background", "id": "background_gradient", "label": "Background gradient" },
    { "type": "color", "id": "text_color", "label": "Text", "default": "#1a1a1a" },
    { "type": "color", "id": "heading_color", "label": "Heading" },
    { "type": "color", "id": "card_background", "label": "Card background", "default": "#ffffff" },
    { "type": "color", "id": "card_text_color", "label": "Card text", "default": "#1a1a1a" },
    { "type": "color", "id": "label_background", "label": "Image label background", "default": "#ffffff" },
    { "type": "color", "id": "label_text_color", "label": "Image label text", "default": "#1a1a1a" },
    { "type": "color", "id": "verified_color", "label": "Verified badge", "default": "#1f7a52" }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "review",
      "name": "Review",
      "settings": [
        { "type": "header", "content": "Before / after" },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": "One file holding both frames, split at exactly 50%, square overall (1:1) so each half is a portrait rectangle. Do not use an image with the words BEFORE or AFTER printed into it — the labels below are text so they can be translated."
        },
        { "type": "image_picker", "id": "image", "label": "Before/after image (square, split 50/50)" },
        { "type": "image_picker", "id": "image_mobile", "label": "Image (mobile)" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "before_label", "label": "Before label", "default": "Before" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "after_label", "label": "After label", "default": "After" },
        { "type": "header", "content": "Customer" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "author", "label": "Customer name" },
        { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_verified", "label": "Show verified badge", "default": true },
        { "type": "text", "id": "verified_label", "label": "Verified badge text", "default": "Verified Customer" },
        { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_rating", "label": "Show rating", "default": true },
        { "type": "range", "id": "rating", "label": "Rating", "min": 1, "max": 5, "step": 1, "default": 5 },
        { "type": "header", "content": "Review" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "title", "label": "Review title" },
        { "type": "richtext", "id": "content", "label": "Review text" },
        { "type": "header", "content": "Product reviewed" },
        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": "Pick the product and the thumbnail, name and link fill themselves in. Use the three fields below it only when the review points somewhere a product picker cannot reach, such as a collection."
        },
        { "type": "product", "id": "product", "label": "Product" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "product_prefix", "label": "Prefix", "default": "Reviewing" },
        { "type": "image_picker", "id": "product_image", "label": "Thumbnail override" },
        { "type": "text", "id": "product_text", "label": "Name override" },
        { "type": "url", "id": "product_url", "label": "Link override" }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "presets": [{ "name": "Review before/after", "category": "Media" }]
}
{% endschema %}
